<title>ESTONIA: ESTONIA - FARMA SIGNS RUSSIAN FACTORY DEAL.</title>
<headline>ESTONIA - FARMA SIGNS RUSSIAN FACTORY DEAL.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tallinna Farmaatsiatehas said on Friday it had signed an agreement with a Russian company to set up a drug packaging factory near Moscow.</p>
<p>The share capital of the new factory, AS Mostal, is $100,000 and Farmaatsiatehas owns 60 percent of its shares, it added in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The work is already in process,&quot; Priit Kivi, the company's chairman, was quoted as saying in the statement.</p>
<p>The maximum production capacity of the factory is $5 million.</p>
<p>Farmaatsiatehas started cooperation with its Russian partner, the state company Medical Chemistry Center, in 1946.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
